course: dictionary
lesson: 6300
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word moral is a good example. «Everything's got a moral, if only you can find it,» says the Duchess. Here moral is the lesson a story teaches.
explain: Moral can also be a describing word, an adjective. «A moral choice» is a choice about what is right and wrong. «A very moral person» means someone who is good, honest and fair. Ask yourself: is the word describing a person or thing, or naming a lesson? The sentence will show you.
explain: Moral support is a different meaning again. It means help by being there and encouraging someone, not by doing the job for them. Morals, in the plural, means a person's beliefs about right and wrong.
fact: A word can have several meanings, and the context shows which one is meant.
fact: As a noun, «moral» means the lesson a story teaches, as in «the moral of the story».
fact: As an adjective, «moral» means to do with right and wrong, or good, honest and fair.
fact: «Moral support» means help by being there and encouraging someone, not by doing the job for them.
fact: A fable is a short story, often with animals, that teaches a moral. «Moral courage» means standing up for what is right, such as owning up to a mistake.
exercise: «Everything's got a moral, if only you can find it.» What is a moral here? | A prize for the fastest runner | A map of the story | *A lesson a story teaches | A type of animal in a fable
exercise: «She showed moral courage by owning up to breaking the window.» What does moral courage mean? | Hiding the truth so nobody is upset | *Standing up for what is right, even when it is hard | Being loud and bossy | Running very fast to escape
exercise: Sam says, «I'll give you moral support while you practise your speech.» What does moral support mean? | *Help by being there and encouraging you | Doing the whole speech for you | Taking your place on stage | Giving you a prize for your speech
test: Ella says, «Being moral means always telling the truth, even when it's hard.» Which meaning of moral is she using? | Moral support | Wet and grey | *Good, honest and fair | A lesson in a story
test: «The morals of the village were strict.» What does morals mean here? | *A person's or group's beliefs about right and wrong | Cheering for the winner | The lesson of a fable | A tiny tortoise
exam: In the sentence «A fable is a short story, often with animals, that teaches a moral», what does moral mean? | *The lesson the story teaches | A race between a tortoise and a hare | The best character in the story | A rule about how to behave in class
